00:21:09.880 --> 00:21:12.040
additional impervious surface?

00:21:19.160 --> 00:21:21.080
>> I think

00:21:25.045 --> 00:21:26.005
I don't know.

00:21:26.565 --> 00:21:27.125
Put

00:21:27.525 --> 00:21:31.445
those words there because that's

00:21:32.165 --> 00:21:33.445
what you recommended.

00:21:33.445 --> 00:21:34.725
And I think that is

00:21:35.820 --> 00:21:37.820
when we went through various examples,

00:21:39.420 --> 00:21:42.220
mitigating the roof and the driveway was

00:21:42.380 --> 00:21:43.740
a pretty significant

00:21:46.140 --> 00:21:49.500
contribution there. It is. And so

00:21:49.695 --> 00:21:53.695
I was happy capturing that on those one or two

00:21:55.055 --> 00:21:59.135
new lots. And one of the goals here is to keep

00:21:59.615 --> 00:22:00.495
it simple,

00:22:01.535 --> 00:22:03.375
keep it effective,

00:22:03.775 --> 00:22:04.575
and

00:22:04.860 --> 00:22:06.620
didn't want to get too much harder

00:22:06.940 --> 00:22:07.900
than that.

00:22:08.940 --> 00:22:16.700
With the one new lot, you know, we're getting pushed back. The people didn't want to mitigate that. They were giving us all kinds of rationale for,

00:22:17.020 --> 00:22:19.820
you know, running down towards the road, not to the lake. And

00:22:20.935 --> 00:22:30.455
as I look there, you know, it it the torturous path that it does take before it gets to the lake does allow a lot of time for runoff.

00:22:30.695 --> 00:22:36.560
Okay. That's fine then. Yeah, I think there's only two or three lots that this will apply to.

00:22:37.280 --> 00:22:38.960
And my goal is to get the

00:22:40.640 --> 00:22:45.680
regulations into effect before the people with that lot there might come

00:22:45.680 --> 00:22:47.760
to Jim with his building permit request.

00:22:48.845 --> 00:22:50.925
So anyhow, that's why that's there.

