here's the letter I got.

00:33:52.925 --> 00:33:53.805
I

00:33:53.805 --> 00:33:54.365
think

00:33:55.005 --> 00:33:56.205
it implements

00:33:56.285 --> 00:33:57.565
pretty easily.

00:33:59.725 --> 00:34:01.245
I'll read it out loud

00:34:02.525 --> 00:34:06.765
because that gives me time to think you guys can read

00:34:06.220 --> 00:34:07.820
and listen at the same time.

00:34:08.380 --> 00:34:11.420
So the section 7.7.2,

00:34:11.420 --> 00:34:13.420
which is Andover Lake A Zone,

00:34:14.380 --> 00:34:21.340
states that a principal structure shall be required to install septic system approved by Eastern Highlands Health District complying with

00:34:21.755 --> 00:34:23.275
Connecticut state code.

00:34:23.355 --> 00:34:26.795
You can see your ebook. It lists the conditions.

00:34:27.355 --> 00:34:27.835
>> And

00:34:28.155 --> 00:34:40.020
then the next paragraph he says, the local director of health may require expansion of the existing sewage disposal system or installation of new sewage disposal system at the time of the change in use

00:34:41.380 --> 00:34:51.940
of those properties whenever the proposed change in use results in more than 50% increase in design flow. And design flow seems to be the buzzword that he was looking for.

00:34:53.595 --> 00:34:59.835
And it talks about design flow means the anticipated daily discharge from a building is determined in accordance with

00:35:00.075 --> 00:35:01.595
some other tech standards.

00:35:03.195 --> 00:35:09.250
And it goes on to discuss what the design flow is for various bedrooms of houses there.

00:35:09.490 --> 00:35:13.490
So I think what he's telling me is to take the paragraph

00:35:13.490 --> 00:35:14.130
that

00:35:15.010 --> 00:35:17.970
we had there and just add the words

00:35:18.290 --> 00:35:21.570
when the project design flow exceeds 50%

00:35:21.890 --> 00:35:23.010
and these four

00:35:23.775 --> 00:35:25.375
items down here,

00:35:26.415 --> 00:35:27.215
and then

00:35:28.095 --> 00:35:30.335
this one, you know, number five replaces

00:35:30.335 --> 00:35:31.935
the

00:35:41.330 --> 00:35:43.410
seven items that we had

00:35:44.290 --> 00:35:45.090
that

00:35:46.210 --> 00:35:46.930
were in there.

00:35:50.725 --> 00:35:52.885
And so based on his recommendation,

00:35:54.005 --> 00:35:55.525
I was just going to

00:35:59.205 --> 00:36:03.925
add when the project design flow exceeds 50% to the title,

00:36:04.500 --> 00:36:08.740
conditions requiring a new appropriate upgraded septic system

00:36:08.900 --> 00:36:12.020
when the project design flow exceeds 50%.

00:36:13.060 --> 00:36:13.780
And then

00:36:14.500 --> 00:36:15.620
take out our

00:36:16.020 --> 00:36:18.900
seven things and put his four in

00:36:20.875 --> 00:36:21.595
there

00:36:22.075 --> 00:36:23.435
or five rather.

00:36:23.595 --> 00:36:25.275
>> Okay, I have a question.

00:36:26.315 --> 00:36:30.875
How were our seven developed? Did we do those or were those John Valentes?

00:36:31.275 --> 00:36:32.475
>> They were

00:36:33.035 --> 00:36:34.235
John Valentes

00:36:34.380 --> 00:36:36.700
And again, we borrowed the

00:36:37.820 --> 00:36:38.780
regulations

00:36:38.780 --> 00:36:40.380
heavily from Columbia's,

00:36:40.380 --> 00:36:41.980
but Columbia did not have

00:36:42.460 --> 00:36:43.260
any

00:36:43.260 --> 00:36:44.700
septic system

00:36:45.740 --> 00:36:52.915
regulations in their lake racks. And so I don't know if he made these up or came through,

00:36:53.475 --> 00:36:56.995
you know, he got them from someplace else, I've got no idea.

00:36:58.435 --> 00:37:00.675
I do know that we talked

00:37:00.675 --> 00:37:03.395
about it a lot and the goal

00:37:03.820 --> 00:37:04.780
is to

00:37:05.180 --> 00:37:07.020
get all these outdated,

00:37:08.460 --> 00:37:12.380
not compliant septic systems to meet state code today.

00:37:13.020 --> 00:37:13.580
>> Okay.

00:37:14.940 --> 00:37:17.660
Thad or someone from his

00:37:17.775 --> 00:37:20.815
agency would be the person who would be permitting

00:37:20.895 --> 00:37:22.895
the septic tank? Yes.

00:37:23.295 --> 00:37:24.095
Okay.

00:37:24.095 --> 00:37:27.615
That being the case, that makes a lot of sense, what you're saying. Yep.

00:37:28.015 --> 00:37:28.735
>> And again,

00:37:29.055 --> 00:37:32.015
as we develop these, we spent some time talking about

00:37:32.400 --> 00:37:38.800
is the right height above the water table 12 inches or 18 inches. We started out with 12.

00:37:39.040 --> 00:37:42.480
We increased that to 18 inches above the water table

00:37:43.040 --> 00:37:43.920
to be

00:37:44.640 --> 00:37:45.520
more restrictive,

00:37:45.705 --> 00:37:47.625
but also consistent

00:37:47.625 --> 00:37:52.985
with the Connecticut Health Code. Why don't we we're around the lake. Why don't we expect

00:37:54.265 --> 00:38:00.850
a septic system to be full compliance with code? And so we changed that. We stuck with the 50%

00:38:01.010 --> 00:38:04.290
size thing because that's consistent with the health code. So

00:38:04.770 --> 00:38:06.210
essentially, we're just saying

00:38:07.010 --> 00:38:09.250
we want it to meet

00:38:09.730 --> 00:38:10.530
